module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_attempt_crashed_between_state_init_and_container_start_is_unrecoverable

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

// Consumer: directory-derived recurring_failure_mode.roster, projected by
// gunbc.design_ledgers.expected_design_failure_modes_md through docs_projection_gate.
data an_attempt_crashed_between_state_init_and_container_start_is_unrecoverable: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_attempt_crashed_between_state_init_and_container_start_is_unrecoverable" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an attempt writes durable initiation state (placement record, attempt pointer, or equivalent) and can stop before the session container that is supposed to inhabit that state starts, and there is no modeled reconciliation that finishes or rolls back both sides of that pair. HARM: the next belt pass cannot tell orphaned state from a live session, so recovery is operator surgery rather than a typed repair (DESIGN section 4b found at mitigatable).",

    "OCCURRENCE, 2026-10-11, srv1 workspace bring-up findings ledger F20/F21, operator review of source pinned to main at acc218340ed6e24a9ad06c550a5494307d0320bb (a source review that did not rerun srv1). belt_session_container_create writes the placement record (session_placement_record_write) then starts the unit (harness-unit-start). A crash between those steps leaves a grant and record with no container. Moving the record write after container creation only swaps the crash gap: then a started unit can exist with no record. Recovery is further incomplete because belt_created_session_cleanup_detail knows only tmux_kill_session_argv_for_instance, while a systemd unit container is a different population. The shared operation needs an activation identity and reconciliation over both sides, not a chosen order of two unlinked effects. Roadmap leaf cc-lifecycle-ownership.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: this is not a launch refusal before any durable write (BeltPlacementRefused / LaunchNoPlacementGrant), which is already a typed stop. It is not a later crash after the container is independently observed running. It is the unreconciled pair of initiation-state vs container-start. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- both sides are modeled facts and an incomplete pair can be a named arm. NEXT TRIGGER: create-or-recover is one identity whose observe/decide/apply/readback either yields a started container matching the initiation state or a rolled-back absence, with a discriminating crash between the two writes going red until that identity exists.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_session_container_create", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_created_session_cleanup_detail", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
